  "worked_solution": "The given expression is a quotient of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $4!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n4!=4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=24.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4!}{0!} & =\\frac{24}{1}=24\\end{aligned}\n$$",
